/-!
# Original 15.2.23 for the chosen-plane escape

The local reductions and actual block actions exclude all chi-blocks and
the NI ≤ MI branch. The component modules construct the original Omega
marking, normalize the escaping component, and exclude the complete marked
catalogue on its full moved section. Corrected SmallActionsSource supplies
the literal residual and quotient conventions in the linear branches.

`PlaneUniquenessPreceding.source_15_2_23` proves
`generalizedFitting I ≠ pCore 2 I` for the original escaping I. The only
explicit additional inputs are the earlier HStar quotients, Kc orbit,
restricted-action alternative and marked plane inverter. Their original
producers and final discharge remain with the plane-uniqueness assembly.
The legacy SmallActions APIs remain available, and the source proof uses
the corrected declarations.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.2.23, printed pp.1115--1117; refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/
